---
description: "Accessibility basics — applies to any user-facing frontend UI code"
alwaysApply: false
globs: ["**/*.tsx", "**/*.jsx"]
---

- Use semantic HTML elements (`button`, `nav`, `label`, headings in order) instead of generic `div`/`span` with click handlers.
- Every interactive element must be keyboard-navigable and focusable — don't rely on hover/click-only interactions.
- Images need meaningful `alt` text (or explicitly empty `alt=""` for purely decorative ones).
- Form inputs need associated labels, not just placeholder text.
- Check color contrast for text against its background meets basic readability — don't rely on color alone to convey state (errors, success, required fields).
